course: dictionary
lesson: 11808
title: Biannual: twice a year
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Biannual» looks long, but its parts help. «Bi» means two, and «annual» means yearly, so «biannual» means happening twice a year.
explain: Read this: «My dentist gives me a biannual check-up, so I see her twice a year.» The words twice a year are the clue. Swap in your meaning: a twice-a-year check-up still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Here is another: «Our school sends a biannual newsletter to every family.» A newsletter that comes twice a year is a sensible idea, so the meaning fits the sentence.
fact: «Biannual» means happening twice a year.
fact: «Bi» means two, and «annual» means yearly.
fact: «Biannual» is an adjective, and «biannually» is the adverb: «The club meets biannually.»
fact: In maths problems, «biannual» can mean 2 times in 12 months, usually about every 6 months.
fact: Do not mix up «biannual» with «annual», which means once a year.
exercise: «My dentist gives me a biannual check-up.» What does biannual mean? | Happening only once, never again | Happening every day | Happening once a week | *Happening twice a year
exercise: «The library holds a biannual book sale.» How many book sales happen in a year? | Twelve | *Two | Four | One
exercise: Which word means once a year? | monthly | daily | biannual | *annual
test: «Our school sends a biannual newsletter to every family.» How often do families get the newsletter? | Every day | Once a week | *Twice a year | Once a year
test: «The bus company checks its buses biannually.» What does biannually mean? | Every two years | *Twice a year | Only in winter | Every day
exam: «The museum opens a biannual exhibition in spring and autumn.» How many exhibitions happen in a year? | One | Twelve | Four | *Two
